// Hello on Windows: a program in the language's own names, printed as LLVM IR
// and linked against kernel32 alone, with no C runtime (docs/spec/llvm.md §2).
//
//   build -target=windows -o hello.exe examples/native/hello-win.oro
//
// Win32 has no `print`. It has WriteFile over bytes, and lib/win/print.oro is the
// program that stands where `fmt.Println` stands on Go: written in the language,
// out of WriteFile and GetStdHandle, each declared as Win32 has it.
use win/print

export fn main() { print.print_str("hello from oroboros") }
